From 4bddc18649ac0ffd7ec6647df21e727786f13d66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:34:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Font b: our font drawn in the game's style is the default
 (FONT=b)

src/main/font_b.h (tools/font/b.txt, fontgen.py font-header b): 11 rows, one baseline (row 8), 1-pixel stems, the 79
US codes, the 44 extra glyphs and the four buttons. With it every species name (MetalGreymonVaccine 109 px) and item
name (93 px) fits its field as drawn, so measureStringMode/fitStringMode/drawStringMode/textFitCode draw every name
with drawString and the tight and condensed modes, FIT_STRIP and the condensed table are left out of a b build.
Also: the 0x16 position code clears from the next cell (it erased the last letter of a shop item), and the Yes/No rows
of the save screens are laid out in the original's cells.
---
 Makefile                  |   2 +-
 include/dw/font.h         |   1 +
 src/main/font.c           |  54 +++++++++++++++
 src/main/font_b.h         | 138 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/main/main_menu.c      |  20 +++---
 src/main/script_textbox.c |   3 +-
 6 files changed, 205 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/main/font_b.h

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 8bbba30..65a21a1 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ $(shell mkdir -p $(GEN_DIR); printf '#define FPS %s\n' '$(FPS)' > $(GEN_DIR)/fps
 #   original  the US font on its 4-pixel grid: the original code and glyphs, byte for byte;
 #   a         the US letters placed to the pixel (src/main/font_a.h, tools/fontgen.py);
 #   b         our font redrawn in the game's style, placed to the pixel (src/main/font_b.h, tools/font/b.txt).
-FONT ?= original
+FONT ?= b
 ifeq ($(filter $(FONT),original a b),)
 $(error FONT=$(FONT): the font must be original, a or b)
 endif
